Title: HAL_RTCEx_BKUPErase and HAL_RTCEx_BKUPBlock_Enable erroneously use "WRITE_REG" instead of "WRITE_BIT"

Body:
In file stm32u5xx_hal_rtc_ex.c, functions HAL_RTCEx_BKUPErase and HAL_RTCEx_BKUPBlock_Enable use the WRITE_REG macro instead of WRITE_BIT. This results in the entire TAMP->CR2 register being reset, which I do not believe is an intended side-effect of these functions.


void  HAL_RTCEx_BKUPErase(RTC_HandleTypeDef *hrtc)
{
  UNUSED(hrtc);
  WRITE_REG(TAMP->CR2, TAMP_CR2_BKERASE);
}

void  HAL_RTCEx_BKUPBlock_Enable(RTC_HandleTypeDef *hrtc)
{
  UNUSED(hrtc);
  WRITE_REG(TAMP->CR2, TAMP_CR2_BKBLOCK);
}


Suggestion is to change these WRITE_REG to SET_BIT as below:



void  HAL_RTCEx_BKUPErase(RTC_HandleTypeDef *hrtc)
{
  UNUSED(hrtc);
  SET_BIT(TAMP->CR2, TAMP_CR2_BKERASE);
}

void  HAL_RTCEx_BKUPBlock_Enable(RTC_HandleTypeDef *hrtc)
{
  UNUSED(hrtc);
  SET_BIT(TAMP->CR2, TAMP_CR2_BKBLOCK);
}

Comments:
[ALABSTM - 2025-09-05T14:21:24Z]
Hi @sk-waymont,

Looks like you're right. Thank you for this heads-up. the WRITE_REG() is defined at the [CMSIS](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/cmsis-device-u5/blob/6e67187dec98035893692ab2923914cb5f4e0117/Include/stm32u5xx.h#L181) level as shown below:

c
#define WRITE_REG(REG, VAL)   ((REG) = (VAL))


Instead, it should be replaced by the SET_BIT() macro defined as below:

c
#define SET_BIT(REG, BIT)     ((REG) |= (BIT))


Let's have this fixed. I'll log an internal tracker.

With regards,

